{
  "state": {
    "repo": "rails/rails",
    "commit": "fddf74bea9",
    "message": "Remove unnecessary `defined?` check for RubyVM::YJIT.enable

Since Rails main branch now requires Ruby 3.3.0,
`RubyVM::YJIT.enable` is always available and the `defined?` guard is no longer necessary.

```ruby
$ ruby -ve 'p defined?(RubyVM::YJIT.enable)'
ruby 3.3.0 (2023-12-25 revision 5124f9ac75) [x86_64-linux]
"method"
```

Refer to
https://github.com/rails/rails/pull/56511

https://www.ruby-lang.org/en/news/2023/12/25/ruby-3-3-0-released/
> Add RubyVM::YJIT.enable that can enable YJIT at run-time"
  },
  "model": "jev-latest",
  "questions": {
    "claim": {
      "type": "noul",
      "instructions": "The author of this commit wrote: "Remove unnecessary `defined?` check for RubyVM::YJIT.enable". Taking "unnecessary" literally, does the claim hold as written?"
    }
  }
}

